{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009660-2e-possessing-by-shadow-name-persona","id":1009660,"title":"[2E] Possessing by Shadow Name Persona","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-29T00:04:58-08:00","id":1009660,"title":"[2E] Possessing by Shadow Name Persona","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=1009342#post1009342\">Promethea comics</a> give me cool idea for characters \u2018usablity\u2019 \u2013 that mages can invoke their Shadow Name Persona as some ephemeral being possessing them ( probably Goetia from Astral ). What could be benefits and dangers of doing things like that? What kind of Influences can we talk about? What would be spells needed for doing things like that? Let the discussion begins! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T00:45:10-08:00","id":1009666,"title":"","content":"A conjunctional spell of Prime + Spirit or Mind, perhaps? Or maybe an Add Prime option to the Possession spell. It seems that spells in 2e prefer &quot;Optionally add Arcanum to a stand-alone spell&quot; to &quot;Require multiple Arcana from the beginning&quot; approach in multi-Arcana spells.<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't be surprised if one's Shadow Name has a tangible presence within the Oneiros. It's a huge part of their psyche, after all. But considering how summoning Goetia from the Oneiros work, summoning one would mean that you'd effectively remove your own Shadow Name during the manifestation. Which would probably remove your access to the Nimbus as well, and maybe even your Praxes, since they are all covered under &quot;Your Magical Persona&quot;. <br /> <br /> As for the Goetia itself, I assume it would be Resonant with and have Influence over the mage's Nimbus, and have custom Numina replicating the mage's Praxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T00:55:22-08:00","id":1009668,"title":"","content":"Crackpot Theory:<br /> Some of the Supernal Beings are literally this - Shadow Names that literally came to life, symbols that became so clear they crystalized into new lifeform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:19:10-08:00","id":1009675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009660-2e-possessing-by-shadow-name-persona?p=1009668#post1009668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crackpot Theory:<br /> Some of the Supernal Beings are literally this - Shadow Names that literally came to life, symbols that became so clear they crystalized into new lifeform.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that how Ascension works?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:20:14-08:00","id":1009676,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:22:20-08:00","id":1009679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009660-2e-possessing-by-shadow-name-persona?p=1009668#post1009668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crackpot Theory:<br /> Some of the Supernal Beings are literally this - Shadow Names that literally came to life, symbols that became so clear they crystalized into new lifeform.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a crackpot theory, that's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=952388#post952388\">basically canon</a>: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=952388#post952388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda.<br /> <br /> The Arthurian World did exist (in some form, it was probably closer to earlier Dark Ages, Arthur laughing as he wrestles bears and smites men versions than after it got lancelotted and romantic fantasied) sometime in post-Roman Britain. It was the pet project of a welsh Silver Ladder Acanthus (and either the founder of or an early member of the Walkers in Mists Legacy) with the Shadow Name of Myrddin (or, in English, Merlin). <b>He achieved archmastery, and his Noumenon, the great act of magic that made him Ascend, was to manipulate Fate to great and then doom the society he built, marking the Symbolism of Arcadia forever.</b> Among the side effects was turning the astral anthropomorphism of Fate into Mordred.<br /> <br /> Then the Arcadian Exarchs deleted the whole thing from the timeline, and history became as we know it. <b>Myrddin, safely Ascended as the very symbol of a cunning bastard, gave no shits.</b><br /> <br /> Tldr - it is a longstanding setting element of Mage, since Tome of the Watchtowers nearly ten years ago, that Merlin was a real mage, that the crystal cave was what he *wanted* (his ascension) and the fall of Camelot was entirely deliberate on his part. It predates Changeling as a gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyway, WRT the OP - I agree with Hermit that someone's Shadow Name would have a presence in their Oneiros, and someone whose Shadow Name persona was strong enough to actually have the Merit would be particularly strong, potentially strong enough to make for a useful Goetia. You could have it manifest as an independent Goetia with Goetic Summons and +1 Reach; having it pilot your body for a bit without separating it from your mind is not quite the same, but it's similar enough that I'd use that spell as a base.<br /> <br /> Its powers could be basically anything, depending on what the shadow persona is. The manifested Shadow Name of a devoutly-religious Theurge dedicated to spreading truth and enlightenment would be quite different from that of a manipulative-trickster Acanthus or Mastigos named for Loki or Anansi or Coyote, which in turn would be different from that of a primal-ecstasy Thyrsus. I imagine that its Rank would depend on the power of the Mage in question and their dots in Shadow Name (if any), but I'm not sure what the best scale would be. Are there rules or official guidelines anywhere for the power level of personal Goetia?<br /> <br /> The benefits and dangers of doing something like that are basically the same thing, I think - this would be a being entirely dedicated to living out the mage's shadow persona, unfettered by other concerns. So it would be impervious to doubt or to the temptations of everyday life (except insofar as those things were part of the shadow persona in the first place) - but on the other hand, it would be impervious to doubt and to the needs of everyday life. If you named yourself Javert and built a shadow persona about finding and punishing the guilty no matter what, and gave it control of your body... best hope no-one you care about turns out to be guilty of any transgression, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:07:26-08:00","id":1009753,"title":"","content":"The concept of a Shadow Name goetia feels... Strange to me. Not at first because it makes a kind of intuitive sense - if your fears and lusts have goetia, why not this part of you? - but then it came upon me that your Shadow Name isn't a &quot;part&quot; of you in the same way those things are; it's grander and more encompassing. Your Shadow Name wouldn't spawn a single goetic entity; it'd spawn whole sections of your Oneiros. When a Mage delves into the Astral, more often than not, their Shadow Name defines their appearance.<br /> <br /> Your Shadow Name isn't a piece of you any more than your normal name is; it IS you. It is your symbol of who you really are. It's not a game of pretend; it is the symbol that you have chosen to weave into the core of your very being.<br /> <br /> You might summon goetia representing specific ideas within your Shadow Name - if you took the name Odin, you might conjure a lust for knowledge, cunning, love of monocles... - but the whole thing can't be summoned because the whole thing is you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:02:27-08:00","id":1009819,"title":"","content":"If you consider your Shadow Name to be a distinct adopted persona, separate from the &quot;normal&quot; you, then it could ostensibly have a representative goetia.<br /> <br /> I suppose it depends on whether the Mage in question <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ceca1JCRQbA\" target=\"_blank\">refers to himself as in his head is Bruce or as Batman.</a><br /> <br /> In the games I've played in, the Shadow Name tends to be reflected heavily in the Daimon, due to the whole &quot;who I desire to be&quot; aspect of the Daimon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 11-29-2016, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:19:06-08:00","id":1009844,"title":"","content":"I feel like that concept comes from thinking about the Shadow Name the wrong way. Your Shadow Name is not this alter ego you develop; it's not some second identity equal or subservient to the first. Awakening is categorically the demise of your Sleeping self (as any Moros will attest). A developed Shadow Name is more representative of you than your birth name. The piece of you that does magic is your soul, and it is so distinct from your old self as to weaken the sympathy between the two.<br /> <br /> Unless your Shadow Name is nothing more than an occult pseudonym, it is more you than any other name you answer to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:37:45-08:00","id":1009856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009660-2e-possessing-by-shadow-name-persona?p=1009844#post1009844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless your Shadow Name is nothing more than an occult pseudonym, it is more you than any other name you answer to.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can change it few times in life, to completely different beings. I think that you are here exaggerating 'Shadow Names likes to fulfill themselves' thing. Shadow Name can be your ( temporary ) Destiny's goal, but are not your 'true reality self'. You too much listen to Silver Ladder mambo-jambo about Atlantis. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-29-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:46:34-08:00","id":1009859,"title":"","content":"Changing a Shadow Name is representative of a significant life event. It isn't done casually. When you change your Shadow Name, you're saying that you have changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:50:35-08:00","id":1009862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009660-2e-possessing-by-shadow-name-persona?p=1009859#post1009859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing a Shadow Name is representative of a significant life event. It isn't done casually. When you change your Shadow Name, you're saying that you have changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you still <b>can</b> change Shadow Name. If Name was your 'true reality self', as you are describing it, it would not be possible to change once chosen Shadow Name. It's pseudonym and occult tool, not 'true reality about yourself' ( even if Silver Ladder says other thing on that ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T11:22:33-08:00","id":1009871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009660-2e-possessing-by-shadow-name-persona?p=1009862#post1009862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you still <b>can</b> change Shadow Name. If Name was your 'true reality self', as you are describing it, it would not be possible to change once chosen Shadow Name. It's pseudonym and occult tool, not 'true reality about yourself' ( even if Silver Ladder says other thing on that ).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow Name is a magical representation of the Mage's identity after the Awakening. If the Mage goes through another life changing event (or just naturally developed) then a new Shadow Name would be more representative. So changing a Shadow Name works despite being so closely tied to the soul. So nothing Axelgear said is a contradiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Grammar 11-29-2016, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T12:06:19-08:00","id":1009883,"title":"","content":"What Tessie said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T12:06:52-08:00","id":1009884,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ek6jgeF.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't know how much it have changed from 1E but I've recently read Mage Noir which talks about Shadow Names and identities. Mages use it as a nickname (which still is your Magical Self). For example you can have a name for your sentinel job, for working in your magical shop and for your archeomancing hobby when you don't want them to mix up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-29-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T12:52:53-08:00","id":1009902,"title":"","content":"I'm not terribly well-read in 1E so I can't talk about that, but the text about Shadow Names in Chapter 8 (page 292) is very clear that they are a lot more than just an alias or nickname. Even if the Mage thinks of the Shadow Name as an alias, it will in time become their magical identity.<br /> <br /> On the original topic of this thread, I'm of the opinion that a Shadow Name won't have a singular Goetic representation. There will be Goetia that represents aspects of the Shadow Name, but the primary representation of the Shadow Name would probably be the Oneiros itself. Or the Mage during an astral journey in their own Oneiros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Spelling 11-29-2016, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T13:02:49-08:00","id":1009907,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that Shadow Names<i> idea</i> would be from Temeons. Once mage declare himself on it, his Oneiros shares link to this Temenos Realm of idea behind Shadow Name. And probably Daimon becomes embodiment of Shadow Name itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T13:12:30-08:00","id":1009911,"title":"","content":"What if you take an original Shadow Name with no pre-established cultural ties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T16:04:53-08:00","id":1009983,"title":"","content":"Your Shadow Name isn't from the Temenos, but other people's associations with the name you chose might be there, just as other people's associations with wizardry and magic lurk in Temenotic Realms, where actual occult traditions duke it out in the realm of the soul against LARPers and writers and players of roleplaying games.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Wizards of the Coast is probably responsible for so damned much Astral Pancryptia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T23:42:21-08:00","id":1010074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009660-2e-possessing-by-shadow-name-persona?p=1009911#post1009911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you take an original Shadow Name with no pre-established cultural ties?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do this? I thought idae of Shadow Name in <b>Mage</b> was choosing <i>meaningful</i> Persona. Without cultural establishment, you will not have meaning, yes?<br /> <br /> Either way, in that situation, your Shadow Name would be only part of Daimon in Oniros - if you would make your Shadow Name somehow famous in Sleepers Collective, it would create also Temenos Realm of it, connected to your own Oneiros. Just like in comic book <b>Promethea</b> example. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009660-2e-possessing-by-shadow-name-persona?p=1009983#post1009983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Shadow Name isn't from the Temenos, but other people's associations with the name you chose might be there, just as other people's associations with wizardry and magic lurk in Temenotic Realms, where actual occult traditions duke it out in the realm of the soul against LARPers and writers and players of roleplaying games.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Wizards of the Coast is probably responsible for so damned much Astral Pancryptia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you explain your point? Maybe simplyfing it to work on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Set_(mathematics)\" target=\"_blank\">Sets</a> A, B and a like?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T23:58:37-08:00","id":1010080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009660-2e-possessing-by-shadow-name-persona?p=1010074#post1010074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do this? I thought idae of Shadow Name in <b>Mage</b> was choosing <i>meaningful</i> Persona. Without cultural establishment, you will not have meaning, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not how culture, meaning, or language works.<br /> <br /> &quot;[Common Forename] the [Adjective]&quot; is a valid format of Shadow Name. &quot;[Esoteric Noun]&quot; is a valid format of Shadow Name. &quot;[Mutant Word Formed From Nonsense Syllables That Sounded Appropriate]&quot; is a valid format of Shadow Name. Not everybody borrows a mythological legacy to identify their Truest aspirational self, particularly when Mad Ones aren't barred from having Shadow Names but <i>are</i> barred from the Temenos. Children invent personal languages on a semiregular basis without their personal power ascending to the domain of mankind's gods and idols.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T00:18:31-08:00","id":1010085,"title":"","content":"&quot;Stalin&quot; is a perfect example of super powerful Shadow Name that wasn't rooted in mythology, culture or any other pre-existing thing (basically, it was a nickname based on a word for steel), but has been forged into something incredibly powerful and booming with meaning.<br /> <br /> It started as a very basic and bare bones &quot;something that will make me sound like a man of steel&quot; combined with &quot;sounding similar to Lenin&quot;, but has become a thing in itself. <br /> Real Mages should forge their own Names :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 11-30-2016, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T00:42:31-08:00","id":1010091,"title":"","content":"The sample Shadow Name Rose-thorns-growing doesn't, as far as I know, refer to any previous cultural or historical being or concept. It certainly has meaning since the name evokes images related to the symbolism around rose thorns, but there should be no Temenos representation of that name since it didn't exist before the Mage chose to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}